hadiths[18]{hadithnumber,text}:
"185","Narrated from Umm al-Mu'minin Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ghusl after janabah, he would first wash his hands, then perform wudu as he did for prayer, then insert his fingers into the water and run them through the roots of his hair, then pour three handfuls of water over his head with both hands, and then pour water over his entire body."
"186","Umm al-Mu’minin Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed ablution (wudu) as he would for prayer, except for washing both feet, and he washed his private parts and wherever impurity had touched, then poured water over himself. After that, he moved both his feet from that place and washed them. This was the way the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed the ritual bath (ghusl) after major impurity (janabah)."
"187","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) says that I and the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) used to perform ghusl from one vessel, that is, a bowl (tub) which is called a faraq."
"188","The Mother of the Believers, Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her), was asked about the manner of the Prophet’s (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bathing. She called for a vessel containing about one sa’ (of water), and bathed with it, pouring water over her head, and there was a thick curtain between the Mother of the Believers and the questioner."
"189","A person asked Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) about performing ghusl (ritual bath) — how much water should be used. He replied, ""One sa’ (measure) of water is enough for you."" The person said, ""It is not enough for me."" Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""One sa’ of water was enough for someone whose hair was thicker than yours and who was better than you (meaning the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him)."" Then Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) led us in prayer wearing only a single garment."
"190","Jubair bin Mut'im (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I pour water over my head three times."" And (saying this) he (peace be upon him) gestured with both his hands."
"191","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that when the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) performed ghusl after janabah, he would use something like a vessel, etc., and take it in his hands. He would begin with the right side of his head, then (apply it) to the left side, and then rub both hands in the middle of his head."
"192","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: I used to apply perfume to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he would go to (all) his wives (i.e., fulfill marital relations), then on the next day, while entering into Ihram, he would shake off the traces of the perfume."
"193","´Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to visit all his (wives) within a single hour of the night or day, and they were eleven. In another narration, it is mentioned that there were nine women. So Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked, ""Did the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) have the strength for all of them?"" He replied, ""(Yes, rather)"" we used to say among ourselves that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was given the strength of thirty men."
"194","Narrated by Ummul Momineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her): She said, ""It is as if I am still seeing the shine of fragrance in the parting of the hair of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), while he was in the state of Ihram (i.e., during pilgrimage)."
"195","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed ghusl after janabah, he would wash both his hands and perform wudu as he would for prayer, then he would perform ghusl, running his fingers through his hair with his hand until he was sure that the skin was wet, then he would pour water over it three times, then wash the rest of his body."
"196","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): (Once) the Iqamah for prayer was pronounced and the rows were straightened. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us, and when he stood at his place for leading the prayer, he remembered that he was in a state of Janabah (impurity). He said to us: ""Stay in your places."" Then he returned, performed Ghusl (ritual bath), and then came back to us while water was dripping from his head. Then he pronounced the Takbir (opening Takbir), and we all prayed with him."
"197","Narrated Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""The Children of Israel used to bathe naked, looking at each other, but Musa (Moses, peace be upon him) used to bathe alone. So the Children of Israel said, 'By Allah! Nothing prevents Musa (peace be upon him) from bathing with us except that he is suffering from a hernia (a kind of male disease).' By chance, one day Musa (peace be upon him) went to bathe and placed his clothes on a stone. The stone ran away with his clothes, and Musa (peace be upon him) chased after it, saying, 'O stone! Give me my clothes, O stone! Give me my clothes.' Until the Children of Israel saw Musa (peace be upon him) and said, 'By Allah! Musa (peace be upon him) has no disease.' (The stone stopped), Musa (peace be upon him) took his clothes and began to beat the stone."" Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""By Allah! There are still six or seven marks on that stone from (Musa's) beating."
"198","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""While Ayub (peace be upon him) was bathing naked, golden locusts began to fall upon him, so Ayub (peace be upon him) started collecting them in his garment. Then his Lord called out to him: O Ayub (peace be upon him)! Did I not make you independent of (the need for) what you see? He said: Yes, by Your Majesty (You have made me independent), but I am not indifferent to Your blessings."
"199","Lady Umm Hani bint Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with her) says: I went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in the year of the conquest (of Makkah), and I found him taking a bath, and Lady Fatimah al-Zahra (may Allah be pleased with her) was screening him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Who is this?"" I replied, ""I am Umm Hani."
"200","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met him in one of the streets of Madinah, and Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) was in a state of janabah. (He says:) So I slipped away from him and went to perform ghusl. Then I came back, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Abu Hurairah! Where did you go?"" Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I was in a state of janabah and I disliked sitting with you in a state of impurity. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Subhan Allah! A believer is never impure."
"201","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), ""Can any of us sleep while in a state of major ritual impurity (janabah)?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: ""Yes! When any of you is in a state of janabah, he should perform ablution (wudu) and then sleep."
"202","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""When a man sits between the four corners of his wife and then strives with her (for intercourse), then indeed ghusl becomes obligatory."
